    {
      "title": "Idempotency and Safe Retries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Idempotency and Safe Retries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Idempotent Operations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Idempotent== = N repeats leave the same end state as one",
                "{green:GET, PUT, DELETE} are idempotent",
                "{red:POST} is ==not== idempotent by default"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Idempotency Key",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Client sends a unique `Idempotency-Key` header",
                "Server stores ==key + response==",
                "On a repeat: return the **stored result**, no reprocessing",
                "Insert key with a ==unique constraint== in the same transaction as the side effect",
                "Concurrent duplicates **fail** instead of both running"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q1"
                  ],
                  [
                    "a",
                    "b"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q1": {
                    "text": "Key already stored?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "a": {
                    "text": "Return stored response",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  "b": {
                    "text": "Process + save key in one txn",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q1",
                    "to": "a",
                    "label": "yes"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q1",
                    "to": "b",
                    "label": "no"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Consumers",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Brokers deliver ==at-least-once==, so duplicates arrive",
                "Dedupe by **message ID**",
                "Or use naturally idempotent writes: upsert, `SET status='paid'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Retrying payments (POST) without a key",
                "Retrying without ==exponential backoff + jitter==",
                "Keeping keys forever instead of a ==TTL=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "At-least-once delivery + idempotent handling = ==effectively exactly-once=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Event-Driven Architecture and Pub/Sub",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Event-Driven Architecture and Pub/Sub",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Events and Pub/Sub",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Event",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Says",
                  "Immutable fact, already happened",
                  "Request to do something"
                ],
                [
                  "Name",
                  "Past tense: `OrderPlaced`",
                  "Imperative: `PlaceOrder`"
                ],
                [
                  "Receivers",
                  "Any number",
                  "One intended"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Pub/sub}: publisher sends to a topic, ==every subscribed consumer group== gets a copy",
                "{blue:Queue}: each message goes to ==exactly one== competing consumer"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Log and Reliability",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Topic is split into ==partitions==",
                "Ordering holds ==only within a partition==",
                "Pick the key, e.g. `orderId`, to keep one order in sequence",
                "Consumer groups track ==offsets== and can ==replay=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Transactional outbox",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "One DB transaction",
                    "note": "data + event row",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Relay",
                    "note": "reads outbox",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "note": "publish",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==DLQ==: poison message parked after repeated failures",
                "==Saga==: local transactions plus compensating steps"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Assuming ==global ordering==",
                "Dual write: DB save and publish diverge without an outbox",
                "No DLQ, so one bad message blocks the stream",
                "Changing event schemas without ==versioning=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Order is per partition only, and delivery is at-least-once, so keep consumers ==idempotent==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
